WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
By 2050, about half the people in the

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.560
world may be short-sighted, if current trends continue.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.640
In most of those eyes, the fault is

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.520
tiny: light comes to a sharp point a

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.360
millimetre or so in front of where it

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.800
needs to land.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.520
Other eyes focus perfectly well, but the light

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.600
can't get through clearly.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.960
So how can technology assist visual disorders?

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.806
Light enters the eye through the cornea, its

00:00:26.887 --> 00:00:29.406
clear, curved front, which does most of the

00:00:29.447 --> 00:00:29.926
bending.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.486
The lens behind it bends the light a

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.886
little more and fine-tunes the focus.

00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:37.526
The light should meet at a sharp point

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:40.486
on the retina, a layer of light-sensitive cells

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.686
at the back, which send signals along the

00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:44.446
optic nerve to the brain.

00:00:44.807 --> 00:00:46.966
For a near object, a ring of muscle

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.926
around the lens contracts, the fibres holding the

00:00:50.007 --> 00:00:52.486
lens go slack, and the lens rounds up

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.966
to bend light more.

00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:55.606
That's accommodation.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.553
Clear vision needs the eye's bending power to

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:00.793
match its length.

00:01:01.074 --> 00:01:04.993
In myopia, or short-sightedness, the eyeball is usually

00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:08.433
too long, or the cornea too steeply curved.

00:01:09.074 --> 00:01:10.993
Light from a distant object comes to a

00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:13.473
point in front of the retina, then spreads

00:01:13.554 --> 00:01:16.113
out again, so distant things look blurred.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.313
Light from a near object is already spreading

00:01:19.394 --> 00:01:22.273
as it arrives, so it focuses further back,

00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:24.913
on the retina, and near things look clear.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.513
To remember it: with myopia, you see what's

00:01:28.594 --> 00:01:30.353
near "my" eyes.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:35.086
In hyperopia, or long-sightedness, it's the other way

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:35.646
round.

00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:38.606
The eyeball is usually too short, or the

00:01:38.687 --> 00:01:41.326
cornea too flat, so light would come to

00:01:41.407 --> 00:01:43.086
a point behind the retina.

00:01:43.647 --> 00:01:45.606
Near objects blur most.

00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:48.846
In astigmatism, the cornea is curved more in

00:01:48.927 --> 00:01:51.646
one direction than another, so there's no single

00:01:51.727 --> 00:01:52.806
sharp point.

00:01:53.087 --> 00:01:56.206
And from about the mid-forties, the lens stiffens

00:01:56.287 --> 00:01:58.286
and can't round up for close work.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.486
That's presbyopia, and it's why many people need

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:02.606
reading glasses.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.313
Some faults aren't about focus at all.

00:02:06.554 --> 00:02:08.713
A cataract is a lens that has turned

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:09.353
cloudy.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.793
Proteins in the lens clump together, so instead

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.593
of passing straight through, light is scattered.

00:02:16.154 --> 00:02:19.513
Vision becomes dim and blurred, colours fade, and

00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:20.953
headlights cause glare.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.793
Ageing is the main cause, and sunlight, smoking

00:02:24.874 --> 00:02:26.793
and diabetes can raise the risk.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.913
So the eye might focus perfectly, but the

00:02:30.074 --> 00:02:33.273
light can't get through clearly, and glasses can't

00:02:33.354 --> 00:02:34.873
clear a cloudy lens.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.580
For a focus fault, change how light is

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.740
bent before it reaches the retina.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.580
Glasses do it from outside the eye.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.860
For myopia, a concave lens, thinner in the

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.460
middle, spreads the light a little, moving the

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.340
focus back onto the retina.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.140
For hyperopia and for reading, a convex lens,

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.020
thicker in the middle, bends light inward, moving

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.140
the focus forward.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:03.140
For astigmatism, a toric lens bends light differently

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.420
in different directions.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.820
Contact lenses do the same job on the

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.460
cornea, moving with the eye for a wider

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.420
clear view.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.860
But worn overnight or cleaned poorly, they can

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.780
let an infection into the cornea.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.800
Laser surgery changes the eye itself.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.280
In LASIK, a thin flap is cut in

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.760
the surface of the cornea and folded back.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.640
A laser then removes a precise amount of

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.760
tissue underneath.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.200
For myopia, it takes more from the centre,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.080
flattening the cornea so it bends light less,

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.240
and the focus moves back onto the retina.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.960
The flap is laid back and heals without

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:40.600
stitches.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.760
But the change is permanent.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.480
It needs a stable prescription and a thick

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.040
enough cornea, it can cause dry eyes and

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.560
glare at night, and it doesn't stop presbyopia,

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.480
because it doesn't change the lens.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.340
For a cataract, the fix is to replace

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.740
the cloudy lens.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.820
Through a tiny cut, ultrasound breaks up the

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.780
old lens, and it's removed.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.500
A folded artificial lens, made of clear plastic,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.140
is slipped in and opens into place.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.020
Light passes through clearly again, and the new

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.140
lens can also correct short- or long-sightedness.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.260
But it can't change shape, so most people

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.860
still need reading glasses.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.660
There's also a small risk of infection.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.460
And it only helps if the retina still

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.260
works.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:31.986
So, like hearing devices, these are matched, not

00:04:32.147 --> 00:04:32.866
ranked.

00:04:33.187 --> 00:04:36.306
Glasses are cheap, safe and easy to change,

00:04:36.387 --> 00:04:39.626
so they suit almost anyone, including growing children.

00:04:39.907 --> 00:04:42.546
Contact lenses suit active people who'll keep them

00:04:42.747 --> 00:04:43.506
clean.

00:04:43.587 --> 00:04:46.546
Laser surgery suits adults with a stable prescription

00:04:46.627 --> 00:04:48.626
who want to be free of lenses.

00:04:48.707 --> 00:04:51.026
Lens replacement is the only one that helps

00:04:51.107 --> 00:04:52.546
a cloudy lens.

00:04:52.627 --> 00:04:55.586
Glasses and corneal surgery leave a long eyeball

00:04:55.907 --> 00:04:56.786
long.

00:04:56.827 --> 00:04:59.506
Cataract surgery removes the clouded lens.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.373
Two exam questions.

00:05:02.654 --> 00:05:03.133
First.

00:05:03.774 --> 00:05:06.893
A nineteen-year-old can read their phone clearly, but

00:05:07.054 --> 00:05:08.973
lecture slides look blurred from the back of

00:05:09.014 --> 00:05:09.533
the room.

00:05:10.094 --> 00:05:12.733
Their prescription has become stronger each year for

00:05:12.814 --> 00:05:13.693
three years.

00:05:14.254 --> 00:05:16.973
Identify the disorder and explain its cause.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.733
Then explain why glasses or contact lenses suit

00:05:20.814 --> 00:05:23.413
them better than laser surgery, for now.

00:05:23.774 --> 00:05:25.213
Pause here to answer.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:36.793
It's myopia.

00:05:36.994 --> 00:05:39.873
The eye's too long or too powerful, so

00:05:39.954 --> 00:05:42.033
light from the distant slides comes to a

00:05:42.154 --> 00:05:44.353
point in front of the retina, while light

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.593
from the nearby phone lands on it.

00:05:46.914 --> 00:05:49.553
Their prescription is still changing, so a laser

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:52.433
correction made now could drift, and it can't

00:05:52.514 --> 00:05:53.153
be undone.

00:05:53.794 --> 00:05:56.273
Glasses or contacts can simply be changed each

00:05:56.354 --> 00:05:56.673
year.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:06:00.113
The classic mistake is choosing laser surgery because

00:06:00.194 --> 00:06:01.073
it's permanent.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:02.780
Second.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.940
A seventy-four-year-old has gradually dim, cloudy vision in

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.660
one eye, and glare from headlights at night.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.740
New glasses haven't helped.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.940
An eye examination finds a cloudy lens and

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:15.900
a healthy retina.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.340
Evaluate lens replacement surgery for this person.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.260
Pause here to answer.

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:34.866
This is a cataract, a clarity fault, which

00:06:34.947 --> 00:06:36.706
is why new glasses didn't help.

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:40.306
Surgery removes the cloudy lens, and an artificial

00:06:40.387 --> 00:06:43.026
lens lets light through to the healthy retina,

00:06:43.107 --> 00:06:44.786
so clear vision can return.

00:06:45.347 --> 00:06:48.226
But reading glasses are usually still needed, and

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.186
there's a small risk of infection.

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.946
On balance, it's a strong choice here.

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:55.826
The classic mistake is thinking laser surgery on

00:06:55.907 --> 00:06:57.426
the cornea would fix it.

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:01.513
So for any vision question, ask where the

00:07:01.594 --> 00:07:02.993
light goes wrong.

00:07:03.274 --> 00:07:05.673
If the focus misses the retina, move the

00:07:05.754 --> 00:07:09.273
focus with glasses, contact lenses or laser surgery.

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:11.913
If the lens is cloudy, replace it.

00:07:12.554 --> 00:07:15.913
Next: what can replace lost kidney function?

00:07:17.134 --> 00:07:18.573
Here are the key notes.

00:07:18.814 --> 00:07:20.733
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:20.814 --> 00:07:21.613
to copy them.
